{"content":[{"c":["REHUM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. One of the 12 Jewish leaders who returned from captivity with Zerubbabel (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.2","r":"Ezra.2.2","rawR":"Ezra.2.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.2","value":"Ezra.2.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.7","r":"Neh.7.7","rawR":"Neh.7.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.7","value":"Neh.7.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 7:7"},", where “Nehum” is apparently a copyist’s error). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Nehum_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Nehum_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Nehum_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Nehum"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Persian commander who, with Shimshai the scribe, wrote to Artaxerxes I, complaining of the Jews’ temple-rebuilding project and promising dire consequences should the project be completed. The king’s response halted construction until the second year of Darius’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.4.8-23","r":"Ezra.4.8-23","rawR":"Ezra.4.8-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.4.8-23","value":"Ezra.4.8-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 4:8-23"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Levite identified as Bani’s son, who helped repair the Jerusalem wall under Nehemiah’s direction (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.17","r":"Neh.3.17","rawR":"Neh.3.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.17","value":"Neh.3.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:17"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Leader who set his seal on Ezra’s covenant (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.10.25","r":"Neh.10.25","rawR":"Neh.10.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.10.25","value":"Neh.10.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 10:25"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Priest who accompanied Zerubbabel (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.3","r":"Neh.12.3","rawR":"Neh.12.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.3","value":"Neh.12.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:3"},"); elsewhere he was called Harim (see ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," mg). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Harim_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Harim_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Harim_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Harim #5"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Rehum","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ezr 2:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.2.2","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.2.2","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.2.2"},{"anchorText":"Neh 7:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.7.7","rawQueryValue":"Neh.7.7","sourceRefExact":"Neh.7.7"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 4:8-23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.4.8-23","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.4.8-23","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.4.8-23"},{"anchorText":"Neh 3:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.17","rawQueryValue":"Neh.3.17","sourceRefExact":"Neh.3.17"},{"anchorText":"Neh 10:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.10.25","rawQueryValue":"Neh.10.25","sourceRefExact":"Neh.10.25"},{"anchorText":"Neh 12:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.3","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.3","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.3"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"73bf105fdf0824851846faa50d59e30266468391e57f4f0758f71cf05cb130d9","sourceItemName":"Rehum","sourceItemOrder":98,"sourceMember":"Articles/R.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Rehum","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Rehum","title":"Rehum","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}